  "statement": "Show that $\\\\sin3\\\\theta-\\\\sin\\\\theta=2\\\\cos2\\\\theta\\\\sin\\\\theta$, and hence solve $\\\\sin3\\\\theta=\\\\sin\\\\theta$ for $\\\\theta\\\\in[0,\\\\pi]$.",
  "solution": "$\\\\sin3\\\\theta-\\\\sin\\\\theta=2\\\\cos(\\\\tfrac{3\\\\theta+\\\\theta}{2})\\\\sin(\\\\tfrac{3\\\\theta-\\\\theta}{2})=2\\\\cos2\\\\theta\\\\sin\\\\theta$. For $\\\\sin3\\\\theta=\\\\sin\\\\theta$: $2\\\\cos2\\\\theta\\\\sin\\\\theta=0$. So $\\\\sin\\\\theta=0\\\\Rightarrow\\\\theta=0,\\\\pi$, or $\\\\cos2\\\\theta=0\\\\Rightarrow2\\\\theta=\\\\tfrac{\\\\pi}{2},\\\\tfrac{3\\\\pi}{2}\\\\Rightarrow\\\\theta=\\\\tfrac{\\\\pi}{4},\\\\tfrac{3\\\\pi}{4}$. Solutions: $0,\\\\ \\\\tfrac{\\\\pi}{4},\\\\ \\\\tfrac{3\\\\pi}{4},\\\\ \\\\pi$.",
